Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  17 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  17 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 23 CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 77 year old female with a left breast mass  biopsied on REMOVED_DATE  diagnosed as infiltrating ductal carcinoma grade REMOVED_DATE                                                                                     FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY    NEGATIVE FOR RESIDUAL CARCINOMA  ELEVEN AXILLARY LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA    BIOPSY SITES WITH FIBROSIS  GRANULATION TISSUE  CHRONIC INFLAMMATION  HISTIOCYTIC AND FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION TO SUTURE MATERIAL  Diagnosis by  Michael Pins  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 08                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast   is a 810 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 3cm unoriented left mastectomy specimen  which includes an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm left axillary tail  and which is partially covered by a REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm skin ellipse  The skin ellipse includes a REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm areola with a 2 0cm in length well healed transverse scar  3 0cm inferior to the nipple  and another 2 0cm in length well healed transverse scar  1 5cm superomedial to the nipple  The remainder of the skin is diffusely tan white  and otherwise unremarkable  The deep resection margin is a smooth plane  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a prior REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm cystic biopsy cavity lined by red tan  grumose material  and surrounded by a rim of intense fibrosis and semifirm sulphur yellow discoloration  The biopsy site is immediately subjacent to the epidermal scar located 3 0cm inferior to the nipple  and approaches to within 0 3cm of the inferior margin  2 2cm of the deep inked margin  4 0cm of the medial margin  6 0cm of the superior margin  and 9 0cm of the lateral margin  Additional sectioning of the breast parenchyma reveals a second prior REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm biopsy site consisting of intense stellate fibrosis and semifirm sulphur yellow discoloration  The biopsy site is immediately subjacent to the second epidermal scar located 1 5cm superomedial to the nipple  and approaches to within 1 0cm of the superior margin  2 5cm of the medial margin  2 5cm of the deep inked margin  5 3cm of the inferior margin  and 12 0cm of the lateral margin  A third REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm area of stellate fibrosis and sulphur yellow discoloration is located midway between the two biopsy sites  2 0cm deep to the nipple  and approaching to within 1 7cm of the superior margin  2 0cm of the deep inked margin  3 0cm of the medial margin  7 0cm of the inferior margin  and 11 5cm of the lateral margin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma consists of mature  lobular  yellow  adipose tissue with interculating fibrous bands  The axillary tail is explored for lymph nodes  eleven lymph nodes are identified in the upper one third of the tail  SECTION CODE  A E  inferior margin and skin  inferior biopsy   F G  superior margin and skin  superomedial biopsy   H  superior margin  fibrous area   I  deep inked margin  inferior biopsy   J  deep inked margin  superomedial biopsy   K  deep inked margin  fibrous area   L  medial margin  en face  M  lateral margin  en face  N  nipple  O T  lymph nodes  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Peter Hedberg  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT    report_end  , Absent.
