   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 15 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm right mastectomy specimen with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm unremarkable skin ellipse containing the nipple  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a centrally located REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm firm white stellate mass  1 0cm anteriorly  there is a second 0 3cm in diameter white retracted nodule with a hemorrhagic core grossly abutting the deep resection margin  The remaining parenchyma is yellow adipose tissue which is grossly unremarkable  Section Code  A E  mass with closest margin  J K  sections from 2nd nodule  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right axillary dissection  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with multiple tan pink lymph nodes dissected and ranging in length from REMOVED_DATE to 1 4cm in length  The nodes are submitted in their entirety in cassettes F through I  Resident  DAVID SABLE  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY PART B  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLARY   EXCISION   report_end  , Absent.
