Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  30 MAY 96 ACCESSIONED ON  30 MAY 96 at 14 55 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 1 OF 3  AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE  SOLID TYPE  WITH PAGETOID EXTENSION INTO OVERLYING EPIDERMIS  REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION MEASURED FROM SLIDES AND PRESENT AT MARGINS  NOTE  No lymphatic or blood vascular invasion is identified  The tumor spans the width of the biopsy in all directions  The relative proportion of in situ versus invasive tumor cannot be ascertained  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 22                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 44 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm white rubbery fragment of tissue attached to a very thin strip of skin  inked  bisected  and entirely submitted in A  Resident  FANG FANG  MD  PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Craig Scott Seidman  M D  David L Berger  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY   report_end  , Absent.
