Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 AUG 98 ACCESSIONED ON  12 AUG 98 at 10 03 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  SPANNING AN AREA OF APPROXIMATELY REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  SEE NOTE  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  INTERMEDIATE GRADE  CONFINED TO THE REGION OF THE MASS  CUTANEOUS HEMANGIOMAS  2   NOTE  Invasion of lymphatic vessels and blood vessels is not seen  The resection margin of the specimen appears free of tumor  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN SIX OF SIX LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD Signed On  17 AUG 98 at 17 34                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 AUG 98 at 09 13 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  and unit number is a left modified radical mastectomy measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm attatched axillary tail  There is an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm tan skin ellipse with an eccentric 2 5cm nipple   areolar complex located 1 0cm from the inferior skin margin  There is a 4 5cm curvi linear surgical incision which is closed by three sutures and located 2 0cm supero lateral to the nipple  The skin ellipse has a REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm tan purple macule  which abuts the infero medial margin and a 0 3cm red pink macule located 2 6cm medial to the nipple  Sectioning beneath the incision reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm defect packed with gauze  Adjacent to this defect  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 6cm irregular  indurated  gritty  gray white to yellow mass  which is focally hemorrhagic  This mass is located 1 5cm from the deep margin and 1 4cm from the skin surface  Located 2 0cm inferiorly from the mass  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm firm  gray white nodule  The remaining breast parenchyma is predominately fatty tissue with a small amount of gritty  soft  gray white fibrous tissue  No other lesions or masses are grossly appreciated or palpated  Multiple lymph nodes are dissected from the axillary tail ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm  The cut surfaces of the nodes range from gray white to yellow and fatty  A representative section of each lymph node is submitted  SECTION CODE  A B  Tumor to deep margin  C E  Tumor  F   Skin overlying tumor  G   Both skin lesions  entirely submitted  H   Small  white nodule  entirely submitted  I   Sections of remaining breast  J L  Lymph nodes  Gross Description by  PAMELA ROMAN                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Absent.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  30 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  30 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 13 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION AND PRESENT AT MULTIPLE INKED MARGINS  SEE NOTE  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW NUCLEAR GRADE  ASSOCIATED WITH THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  NOTE  Perineural invasion is identified  No blood vascular or lymphatic vessel invasion is identified  Diagnosis by  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 17 46                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  A few tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stain