Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  22 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13 20 CLINICAL DATA  Seventy two year old female with needle localization on REMOVED_DATE consistent with infiltrating ductal carcinoma  grade REMOVED_DATE with greater than 95  infiltrating carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  2  BIOPSY SITE  LYMPH NODES  METASTATIC ADENOCARCINOMA  INVOLVING TWO OF SIX LYMPH NODES  NOTE  There is no evidence of residual infiltrating carcinoma or ductal carcinoma in situ in the mastectomy specimen  The margins are free of lobular carcinoma in situ  The metastatic carcinoma has the morphology of ductal carcinoma  similar to the patient s primary tumor  Drs A  Rosenberg and J  O connell have reviewed selected slides and concur with the interpretation  Diagnosis by  Daniel Rubin  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 44                                                                                     ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION Addendum     Three additional lymph nodes have been submitted for histologic review and are negative for tumor  Added by  Daniel Rubin  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 17 53 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh with the patient s name and unit number is a modified radical mastectomy specimen consisting of a right breast with dimensions of 15 x 7 x 10cm  overlying skin ellipse with dimensions 15 x 6cm  and axillary contents 7 x 7 x 1 5cm  Superior and lateral to the unremarkable nipple is a curvilinear scar 2 5cm in length  A firm mass located superolaterally to the nipple contains a 3 x 3cm oblong cavity which begins 1cm superior and lateral to the nipple and extends for 6cm laterally  The wall of the cavity is lined by friable red tan tissue  Surrounding the cavity is firm  light yellow tissue that is surrounded by soft yellow lobulated tissue  The cavity comes to within 0 5cm of the deepest posterior inked margin  The cavity begins 1cm unbeneath the skin scar  The breast parenchyma posterior and medial to the nipple and medial is firm and gray and focally hemorrhagic  The skin and nipple are unremarkable  Six lymph nodes are dissected from the axillary fat pad  The largest is 3 x 1 x 1cm and contains focal green yellow soft tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  Two representative sections of the largest lymph nodes are submitted  The five smaller nodes are submitted in toto  one per cassette  Section Code A F   representative breast parenchyma surrounding cavity G H   representative parenchyma posterior and medial to nipple I   deepest resection margin J   nipple K   largest lymph node L P   smaller lymph nodes in toto  one per cassette  Resident  Rex Neal Smith  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  John Daniel Puskas  M D  James M Fitzgerald  M D  Rex Neal Smith  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST AND AXILLARY NODES   report_end  , Present.
